On top of that, this parkour game even has some decent gunplay and story.

Cyberpunk 2077

7 / 10 (good, I recommend it for players that like action games with RPG elements).

The Positive:
* Excellent voice acting;
* Very good characters;
* Very good graphics and art direction;
* Very beautiful Night City;
* Good main story and good story for the most important side quests;
* Good overall lore of earth and humankind in this alternative dark future;
* Good performance and stability;
* Good soundtrack and sound in effects and ambience;
* Good character customization for ‘’builds’’ and gameplay style (but mainly for fighting);
* Good character customization for body and clothes (but almost useless since we mainly play as FPS);
* The way V interacts in 1st person with the characters is well done, very immersive and cool for us players. It’s done in a ‘’cinematic’’ way when we are in control or not;
* Very good decision to let the players achieve different endings without having to reset the game entirely.

The Neutral:
* Mediocre gameplay at fighting and exploring. Mediocre action and ‘’adventure’’;
* Considerable part of the minor side quests are repetitive and uninspired;
* Mediocre police mechanics;
* Mediocre population mechanics;
* The main quest is too short. I liked it much more than the side quests, but it ended when I wanted more of it;
* Night City is beautiful and huge, but it lacks depth in its routine and main services/infrastructure.

The Negative:
*  The game would be better if it had an alternative solid 3rd person mode, especially because it’s a cyberpunk game with good options for visual customization, just aesthetic or linked to body improvements… It’s a shame a locked 1st person mode to a very customizable V in a dark future where customization is a huge part of human culture. That’s not enough the motorcycle 3rd person camera;
* The RPG mechanical elements linked to V’s roleplaying and choices-consequences are weak;
* V’s origins are poorly linked to V’s journey;
* I couldn’t feel Night City as a real living metropolis; 
* CDPR lies and many broken promises about game features, easily noted even playing at March/2026.

CONCLUSION:
* Cyberpunk 2077 is a good game, worth my time and money.
